Description: Parallel computation and data exchange between R processes on
    the same machine: lock-free channels, work-stealing task pools, and a
    parallel map over 'POSIX' shared memory (Linux, macOS) or 'Win32' file
    mappings (Windows), with the hot path entirely in user space.
    Inter-process communication cheap enough that work can be divided at
    granularities usually reserved for threads. Vectors and data frames
    transfer zero-copy, received as 'ALTREP' views over the shared pages;
    'Apache Arrow' tables and record batches travel as a single frame,
    with zero-copy conversion in both directions. Receives and task
    results integrate with 'later' and 'promises' for non-blocking,
    event-driven applications such as 'shiny'. Channels, pools, and maps
    interoperate with 'pymizu', so a peer or worker can equally be a
    Python process. A complement to 'mirai'; its payload contents
    interoperate transparently with 'mori' shared objects.
